Subject: Re: Is this becoming GNU/LINUX OS/390???? (fwd)

> Thought some of you might be interested what's happening in the Big Blue
> World.

Holy bizarreness, Batman!

The major concern I'd have is whether or not you'll get decent context 
switching times.  Indications are that MVS systems (and their friends) like to 
have big processes that just kind of keep running.  The UNIX approach of 
forking off processes for everything under the sun is liable to have some 
unfortunate effects on performance.

On UNIX, things are "tuned" for having reasonable times to create new 
processes.  MVS, VMS, and NT are all noted for having somewhat "less 
reasonable" costs for starting new processes.  Which is a lot of the reason 
why NT folk are really into threads; they *need* threading to get decent 
performance...

>  Tanx...I would be interesting in hearing any one elses opinion on this.
>  There is a slew of GNU stuff out there.  Is it worth any time?
>  Plus the fact that some of us can barely port our way out of the
>  shower in the morning!!!!!!

I know that if *I* were there *I* would work with it; if there's noone with 
much C skill, getting it all to work may be troublesome.

It certainly sounds crazy, but at least "entertaining" crazy.  The funny thing 
to do would be to try to get Apache running :-) and have an MVS web server 
using UNIX software...  Perl on MVS would be undoubtedly the most entertaining 
thing possible...

