David Alan Gilbert <dg@cogency.co.uk> wrote:

> What does -mieee do? Does it contain a library of exception handlers or does it
> turn the
> exceptions off. (I would kind of expect the kernel to handle denormals, although
> NaN's and Infinities
> I can imagine the user getting).
Specifically, this tells the compiler to generate floating point instructions with the /s (software completion) option. (eg. multsu $f10, $f11, $f12 # multiply registers $f10 by $f11 (t-floating format) with software completion, underflow enabled). If either input contains an invalid value (denormal, NaN, ...) or the result underfloaws or is invalid, generate a trap. The kernel should contain the appropriate code to perform the fixup. (Note: I am not 100% sure of Linux. I am responsible for the Digital Unix kernel floating point completion). 
