From: Calvin Coghlan <CCOGHLAN@dcnhs-wc.edu>
Subject: Re:portmap error 61

Hi,

Hope this helps.

portmap = is a process that keeps track of and finds processes' network
service port if it has one.

RPC = remote proceedure call.  Different meanings depending on usage. 
Programming call for executing code thru a network conection, generally
on a different system.  Also referrs to a process or subprocess that
could be running to accept and/or initiate code calls.  

task of released request still queued!
   a process is attempting to run, it is in a queue.
      generally indicates receiving process/device is not ready.

(task is on xprt_pending)
   the process appears to be a print task for X

