Message-ID: <199801161559.IAA01437@ellpspace.math.ualberta.ca>
Date: Fri, 16 Jan 1998 08:30:25 -0600 (CST)
From: Chad Campbell <campbell@ukans.edu>
Subject: Re: EM86 kernel patch?
In-Reply-To: <Pine.LNX.3.96.980116132915.10892B-100000@bartlet.df.lth.se>

> >            Your kernel does not support 31-bit addressing!
> >            Please apply the EM86 kernel patch and try again. 
> 
> I had that problem too, and never got rid of it. If you get a sollution,
> I'm interested.
Make the following change to /usr/src/linux/include/asm/a.out.h and
recompile.

/*#define STACK_TOP (0x00120000000UL)*/

#define STACK_TOP ((current->personality & ADDR_MAX_32BIT) ? 0x100000000UL : \
((current->personality&ADDR_MAX_31BIT) ? 0x80000000UL : 0x00120000000UL))

