From k125374@cs.tut.fi Wed Dec 17 18:22:18 1997
Message-ID: <199801161405.QAA23866@kaarne.cs.tut.fi>
Date: Fri, 16 Jan 1998 16:05:48 +0200 (EET)
From: Mika Kortelainen <k125374@cs.tut.fi>
Subject: A solution to em86 problems

...

in the pure include/asm-alpha/a.out.h and also with patch-2.0.32
there is the following define:
#define STACK_TOP (0x00120000000UL)

but with 2.0.30 patches it says:
#define STACK_TOP ((current->personality & ADDR_MAX_32BIT) ? 0x100000000UL : \
      ((current->personality&ADDR_MAX_31BIT) ? 0x80000000UL : 0x00120000000UL))

<-- clap -->

I.e. the fix is to change STACK_TOP to the lower definition (which was
in em86 patches for 2.0.30 but not in 2.0.32 or something like that).

	Mika Kortelainen

