From apilos01@utopia.poly.edu Thu Jan 22 04:29:23 1998
Message-ID: <199801220238.VAA01871@alpha1.estabrook.org>
Date: Wed, 21 Jan 1998 18:57:31 -0500 (EST)
From: Aleksandr Pilosov <apilos01@utopia.poly.edu>
Subject: bug/patch in FD_SET macros

On Alpha, FS_SET(fd,n) macros are broken for n%64 >32
Fix: 
change /usr/include/gnu/types.h, definition of __FDMASK from
#define __FDMASK(d)     (1 << ((d) % __NFDBITS))
to
#define __FDMASK(d)     (1UL << ((d) % __NFDBITS))

What happens is that 1 is an int, so it can't be left-shifted more than 32
times, 1UL is unsigned long, and works fine and dandy.

I'm not sure if this list is correct way to report bug/patch for alpha
glibc, but the axplinux-libc@listserv.azstarnet.com seems down.

