And it even makes sense, too... :-)

Before the use of the BIOS emulator, code for each supported VGA device had
to be put into the consoles, since they had to know how to init them (modern
VGAs do *not* normally power up directly into standard VGA mode).

The same was happening for SCSIs, but it took a good bit of time to make
sure that it all hung together correctly; there may be a bit more going
on in there than for a VGA...

--Jay++

